<title>UK: FIC sets $80 mIllion convertible seven-year bond.</title>
<headline>FIC sets $80 mIllion convertible seven-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by lead manager BZW.</p>
<p> BORROWER   FIRST INTERNATIONAL COMPUTER, TAIWAN</p>
<p> AMT    $80 MLN	 COUPON     1.00	MATURITY    12.MAR.04</p>
<p> TYPE   CONVERTIBLE   ISS PRICE  PAR</p>
<p> LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> CONVERSION PRICE     NT$67.98</p>
<p> CONVERSION PREMIUM   12 PCT OVER THE FIVE DAY AVERAGE CLOSING</p>
<p>			    PRICE TO 27.FEB.97 OF NT$60.70</p>
<p> CALL PROVISIONS	CALLABLE FROM YEAR THREE AT PAR SUBJECT</p>
<p>			    TO A 140 PCT HURDLE</p>
<p> PUT PROVISIONS	 PUT ON 30.APR.02 TO YIELD 7.078 PCT</p>
<p>			    ANNUALISED AT 136.1216 PCT</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
